        "id": 1011323
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-08-22T11:26:16Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Confidentiality (don\u0027t disclose to unauthorized parties) is right, but \"no data … into external tools … or AI-assisted analyzers\" is broader than confidentiality and unenforceable — researchers routinely use scanners/static analyzers, many now AI-backed, and a report from someone who used one but found a real bug is still valuable.\n\nCould we narrow this to non-disclosure (no public trackers / unauthorized sharing) rather than a ban on the reporter\u0027s private tooling?",
      "range": {
